course: dictionary
lesson: 9293
title: Many meanings of one word
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, and the context tells you which one to use. «Speak clearly.» means say words out loud. «She speaks French.» means she knows and uses the language.
explain: «Can I speak to your mum?» means have a conversation with her. «Speak to the class» means give a talk to the class. Ask yourself what the sentence is about, then choose the meaning that fits.
explain: To check your choice, swap in another word and see if it still makes sense. «She knows French» fits, so speaks means knows and uses the language here.
fact: Speak means to say words out loud, or to talk.
fact: «Speak clearly» means say your words so that others can understand you.
fact: «Speak up» means say something louder, or say what is wrong so someone can help.
fact: In a waiting room you speak quietly and stay seated, because patients may be ill or worried.
fact: Speak softly around small animals, so they feel safe.
exercise: «She speaks French.» What does speaks mean here? | Shouts at a friend | Says words out loud very loudly | Gives a talk to a group | *Knows and uses the language
exercise: In a doctor's waiting room, how should you speak? | *Quietly, because patients may be ill or worried | Shouting at the nurse | Not at all, ever | Loudly, so everyone hears
exercise: Which sentence uses speak to mean have a conversation? | «She speaks French.» | «Speak softly to the cat.» | *«Can I speak to your mum?» | «Speak clearly.»
test: «The King says «Don't be impertinent» and gets behind Alice as he speaks.» What does speaks mean here? | *Says words out loud | Argues in court | Knows a language | Gives a talk
test: If something is wrong, you should speak up. What does speak up mean? | *Say it out loud so someone can help | Stop talking forever | Whisper to the wall | Stand up and sing
exam: Which meaning fits «speak to the class»? | Say a word quietly | Forget the class | *Give a talk | Know a language
